&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-ONSITE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We unite cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel in a single company – powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open, to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We work with the world&#39;s most valuable brands and have global reach across 100+ markets, with deep local expertise.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our people are the key to our success. We&#39;re committed to fostering a culture of creativity, belonging and continuous learning, attracting and developing the brightest talent, and providing exciting career opportunities that help our people grow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://eur02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwpp.com%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CErica.Durr%40wpp.com%7C9bf4566a65bc46a48ac008de749116ea%7C150b5e663d884dee83f6ed149b727a00%7C0%7C0%7C639076363668176216%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=Q9juosud56XGLThSFZ1NpPZd6FXpJPxV74OeRZWoh%2B4%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;WPP.com.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why we&#39;re hiring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is embarking on a major, multi-year global CRM transformation to create a simpler, more connected and consistent approach to managing our clients and growth opportunities across the organisation. The programme will consolidate CRM platforms and processes, standardise core client, pipeline and opportunity management practices, and strengthen the data, integration and governance foundations needed to provide a trusted global view of our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Global Programme Director, CRM to lead this transformation end to end, turning our ambition into an executable global programme and bringing together business, technology, data, architecture and change teams across agencies and markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible leadership role for someone who can navigate the complexity of a federated global organisation, challenge legacy ways of working and drive the decisions, delivery discipline and adoption needed to establish a common global CRM capability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the global CRM transformation vision, roadmap and delivery strategy, translating strategic ambition into a clear, executable multi-year programme across agencies and markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the consolidation and simplification of CRM platforms and processes, establishing a clear approach to global standardisation while managing legitimate local requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the adoption of common global processes across client and contact management, pipeline and opportunity management, forecasting, client planning and cross-agency collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead programme delivery across CRM product, architecture, data, integrations, security, testing, migration, cutover and deployment, working closely with Enterprise Technology and business leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure CRM integrates effectively with the wider enterprise technology landscape and that client, account, contact and opportunity data is structured, governed and managed consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the integrated programme plan, governance, dependencies, RAID, assurance and stage-gate process, providing clear visibility of delivery confidence, risk, decisions, budget and benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and lead the global deployment, business readiness and adoption strategy, sequencing agencies and markets based on value, readiness, data quality and change capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish robust go/no-go, cutover, hypercare and stabilisation processes to protect business continuity and ensure each deployment is successfully embedded.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the programme business case, budget, forecast and benefits framework, ensuring investment remains linked to measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage system integrators, CRM product partners and other third parties against clear deliverables, commercial commitments, milestones and quality expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the principal programme interface for executive sponsors and senior agency, market, technology and functional leaders, creating alignment and driving timely decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge complexity, local exceptions and assumptions that could undermine the global outcome, balancing business requirements with simplicity, scalability and long-term value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a high-performing, global matrixed programme team spanning programme management, product, process, architecture, data, testing, change and deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create an evidence-led delivery culture built on transparency, disciplined decision-making, early escalation and shared accountability for outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience leading large-scale, multi-year global transformation programmes within a complex, matrixed or federated organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience delivering major enterprise CRM transformation, ideally involving platforms such as Salesforce or Microsoft Dynamics 365.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of how CRM transformation connects technology, business process, operating model, data and organisational change, rather than treating CRM as simply a technology implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience consolidating fragmented platforms or processes and establishing greater global standardisation across multiple businesses, markets or geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programme leadership across areas such as architecture, integration, master data, data migration, testing, security, deployment and business readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of managing complex programme governance, integrated plans, interdependencies, risks, stage gates and executive-level assurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and financial capability, including ownership of significant programme budgets, business cases, forecasting, benefits realisation and vendor performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing system integrators, software providers and strategic delivery partners in complex enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional senior stakeholder leadership, with the presence and credibility to influence executive sponsors, challenge constructively and secure decisions across competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading large, geographically dispersed and matrixed teams across business and technology functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong change and adoption capability, with experience embedding new processes and ways of working and measuring whether transformation has genuinely landed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to translate complex programme, technology and data issues into clear executive-level decisions, risks and trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pragmatic, resilient and outcome-focused leadership style, comfortable operating through ambiguity and making difficult decisions when delivery is at risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desirable&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A recognised programme or project management qualification such as MSP, PgMP or PRINCE2.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRM platform certification or deep delivery experience within an enterprise Salesforce or Microsoft Dynamics 365 environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change management accreditation such as Prosci, or equivalent practical experience leading enterprise-scale adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re open&lt;em&gt;:&lt;/em&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;We are inclusive and collaborative; we encourage the free exchange of ideas; we respect and celebrate diverse views. We are open-minded: to new ideas, new partnerships, new ways of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re optimistic&lt;em&gt;:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;span id=&quot;628d56ad5d8a35dab853e65d9daa237c&quot; class=&quot;editor-module-hl-green-solid&quot;&gt;We believe&lt;/span&gt; in the power of creativity, technology and talent to create brighter futures or our people, our clients and our communities. We approach all that we do with conviction: to try the new and to seek the unexpected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re extraordinary:&lt;/strong&gt; we are stronger together: through collaboration we achieve the amazing. We are creative leaders and pioneers of our industry; we provide extraordinary every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;ll give you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Passionate, inspired people&lt;/strong&gt; – We aim to create a culture in which people can do extraordinary work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale and opportunity&lt;/strong&gt; – We offer the opportunity to create, influence and complete projects at a scale that is unparalleled in the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Challenging and stimulating work&lt;/strong&gt; – Unique work and the opportunity to join a group of creative problem solvers. Are you up for the challenge?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(236, 240, 241);&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WPP is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to particular characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
